    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a high-ceiling lineup led by **Kyle Tucker**, whose 77.80 score represents the gold standard for today\u2019s matchups. Facing McCullers Jr. (4.75 xERA), **Kyle Tucker** is perfectly positioned to capitalize on a favorable platoon split and strong lineup placement. Close behind is **Jackson Merrill** (75.10), who benefits from a prime leadoff spot against Houser; while he faces an elite-tier pop time from the catcher, his dynamic platoon advantage and current form make him an essential play. **Gunnar Henderson** rounds out the elite tier at 74.77, aided by his favorable matchup against P\u00e9rez and a rare \"green light\" opportunity stemming from the pitcher's slow delivery, which significantly boosts his stolen base expectation.\n\nSeveral players see their value buoyed by specific environmental or situational variables. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (67.67) stands out, as his matchup against McClanahan is mitigated by his high xwOBA and a positive platoon edge, while **Andy Pages** (66.49) remains a high-floor start given the combination of a generous xERA from McCullers Jr. and his ability to exploit the same stolen base efficiency windows as **Gunnar Henderson**. On the flip side, **Jacob Wilson** (49.25) presents a marginal start; despite the wind blowing out, he is severely handicapped by facing Wheeler (2.89 xERA), effectively neutralising his potential for meaningful production.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was **Nolan Schanuel**, who finished at 59.14, narrowly missing the cut behind **Liam Hicks** and **Drake Baldwin**. While **Nolan Schanuel** projects well against Schultz, the optimizer favored the specific dynamic platoon upside of the primary catcher slot today. We are also keeping a close eye on **Josh Jung**, who remains benched with a 50.23 score; beyond being projected lower than our active starters, he carries a 45% rain risk that renders him an unnecessary gamble for today\u2019s cap-sensitive roster. We will proceed with the active lineup, prioritizing the aggressive base-running profiles of **Sam Antonacci** and **Brady House** to secure the scarcest category of the week.",
